#!/usr/bin/env python3
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = [
#   "pydantic>=2.7,<3",
# ]
# ///
"""jev_report.py: an HTML report of judge-jev runs (references/report.md). It reads local files only; it never calls
Jev.

quality  One fix run (references/fix-strategy.md): the record's fix workspace, ``.sc/judge-jev/fix/<ID>``. It shows
         what improved and why: each statement a rule fired on in ``base`` and whether it still fires in ``final``,
         the Jev answers that explained it before and after, the candidate step that cleared it, every answer's
         confidence (base hollow, final solid, one tab per question), and the Markdown diff of ``original.md`` to
         ``current.md``. --review FILE adds the author's drift review: the changes kept and discarded, and why.
check    Each location's verdict against the records that govern it, aggregated per record and per location, from a
         check results file (the contract is ``CheckResults`` below). judge-jev has no ``check`` command yet: this mode
         renders that contract so the report exists when the command does.

Rendering: each panel is one strict sc-compose render of templates/<kind>-panel.xhtml.j2 and the page one render of
templates/report.html.j2, which receives top-level arrays and the rendered panels. Only the diff fragments are built
here (escaped text inside <del>/<ins>).

Output: --out DIR receives <name>.html, the sidecar <name>.json and one XHTML panel per unit in <name>/. One JSON
envelope ``{success, data, error}`` on stdout; exit 0 when the report was written, 2 with a typed error
(VALIDATION.INPUT, REPORT.NO_RUNS, SCRIPT.IO, DEPENDENCY.SC_COMPOSE, RENDER.FAILED, SCRIPT.INTERNAL), 130 on interrupt.
"""

